{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he entreated.</b> He multiplied and persisted in prayer." "<b>And was entreated of him.</b> He was constrained and appeased and persuaded toward him. And I say: every expression of עֶתֶר is an expression of persistence and multiplication, as in ״וַעֲתַר עֲנַן הַקְּטֹרֶת״ (Ezekiel 8) — the multiplying of the rising of the smoke; and as in ״וְהַעְתַּרְתֶּם עָלַי דִּבְרֵיכֶם״ (ibid. 35); and as in ״וְנַעְתָּרוֹת נְשִׁיקוֹת שׂוֹנֵא״ (Proverbs 27) — they seem to be multiplied yet are a burden; אנקרי״שרא בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>Opposite his wife.</b> This one stands in this corner and prays, and this one stands in that corner and prays." "<b>And was entreated of him.</b> Of him and not of her — for the prayer of a righteous person son of a righteous person is not like the prayer of a righteous person son of a wicked person. Therefore, of him and not of her (Yevamot 64)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French encresser, 'to increase/multiply'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:29.651719724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}